     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>On Tuesday, 2 August 2016 21:27:39 UTC+8, Phil Chalmers  wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">This is fine, it&#39;s how exploratory factor analysis models are identified (hence, why they need rotation post-estimation). </div><div><br clear=\"all\"><div><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">Phil</span><br></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>\r\n<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Mon, Aug 1, 2016 at 1:09 PM, Oce <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">oce....@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><div>I ran a mirt:<br><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">LLS</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mirt </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mirt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">LLS</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> itemtype </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;graded&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> method </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;QMCEM&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> technical </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">NCYCLES </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">10000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span></div></code></div><br>The coef generated contained a lower diagonal of 0s, does this suggest problems with the model? <br><br><code><span style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">coef(LLS.mirt, simplify = T)$item</span></code></div></div><br>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"715\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:715pt\">\r\n <colgroup><col width=\"65\" span=\"11\" style=\"width:65pt\">\r\n </colgroup><tbody><tr height=\"15\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n\r\n  <td height=\"15\" width=\"65\" style=\"height:15.0pt;width:65pt\"></td>\r\n  <td width=\"65\" style=\"width:65pt\">a1</td>\r\n  <td width=\"65\" style=\"width:65pt\">a2</td>\r\n  <td width=\"65\" style=\"width:65pt\">a3</td>\r\n  <td width=\"65\" style=\"width:65pt\">a4</td>\r\n  <td width=\"65\" style=\"width:65pt\">a5</td>\r\n  <td width=\"65\" style=\"width:65pt\">a6</td>\r\n  <td width=\"65\" style=\"width:65pt\">a7</td>\r\n  <td width=\"65\" style=\"width:65pt\">a8</td>\r\n  <td width=\"65\" style=\"width:65pt\">a9</td>\r\n  <td width=\"65\" style=\"width:65pt\">a10</td></tr></tbody></table><div> ...<br>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> D37 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.897</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.072</span><span style=\"